<p>I'm typing this in Emacs using a completely new config and it's so weird. I've been running Emacs v31 everywhere and thought I'd try leaning on more of the built-in completion behavior, and it spiraled out of control.</p>
<!-- more -->
<p>I ended up looking at <a href="https://github.com/LionyxML/emacs-solo#optional-dependencies">emacs-solo</a> because it's a fancy configuration that only uses built-in packages. It was easy to try out, so I did. And I liked it. I added the necessary-for-me missing components of my old config.</p>
<p>My favorite part is that I went from 143 installed packages to 49 and got rid of hundreds of lines of config that I didn't really need. Also, my startup time was cut in half and is now under 1 second. Nice.</p>
<p>It'll take a minute for everything to burn in and shake out, but so far I don't hate it.</p>
